From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: dcn321: disable DSC power gating

On a Radeon RX 7600 (DCN 3.2.1) driving an HDMI 2.1 sink at 7680x4320@60
over FRL with DSC, the first DSC stream after a cold boot carries no
usable signal: FRL link training reports success and the DSC PPS is
programmed, but the sink sees nothing until any later modeset. The only
difference between the failing first enable and a later working one in
the log is that the first one has to bring the DSC block out of power
gating (dcn32_dsc_pg_control "disable DSC power gate") right before use.

Keep the DSC blocks powered, as dcn314/dcn35/dcn351/dcn36 already do by
default, so the first DSC stream after boot works.

Diagnostic patch, reproduced 3/3 cold boots; measured with drm.debug=0x106
and the HDFury VRROOM's RX status.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn321/dcn321_resource.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn321/dcn321_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn321/dcn321_resource.c
@@ -768,6 +768,7 @@ static const struct dc_debug_options debug_defaults_drv = {
 
 	/*must match enable_single_display_2to1_odm_policy to support dynamic ODM transitions*/
 	.enable_double_buffered_dsc_pg_support = true,
+	.disable_dsc_power_gate = true,
 	.enable_dp_dig_pixel_rate_div_policy = 1,
 	.allow_sw_cursor_fallback = false, // Linux can't do SW cursor "fallback"
 	.alloc_extra_way_for_cursor = true,
